-- title:
--   Spanning sets of Mₙ(A) lift from the residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a finite index set with decidable equality, let $A$ be a commutative local ring, and let $k$ be a field. Let $\pi : A \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism, and let $S$ be a set of $n \times n$ matrices over $A$. Write $X \mapsto X.\mathrm{map}\ \pi$ for the entrywise application of $\pi$, sending $M_n(A)$ to $M_n(k)$. Suppose that the image of $S$ under this map spans $M_n(k)$ as a $k$-vector space, i.e. the $k$-submodule of $M_n(k)$ generated by $\{X.\mathrm{map}\ \pi : X \in S\}$ is the whole of $M_n(k)$. The conclusion is that $S$ itself generates $M_n(A)$ as an $A$-module: the $A$-submodule of $M_n(A)$ spanned by $S$ equals $\top$. No finiteness, Noetherian or completeness hypothesis on $A$ is imposed beyond its being a commutative local ring, and $\pi$ is not required to be the canonical map to the residue field — only surjective onto a field, so that its kernel automatically lies in the maximal ideal.
--
--   This is Nakayama's lemma applied to the finite free module $M_n(A)$: a spanning set of the matrix algebra over the residue field lifts to a spanning set over the local ring. It is used in the construction of trace algebras for deformations of Galois representations, where, via Burnside's theorem, absolute irreducibility of a residual representation yields that the image of a lift spans the full matrix algebra over $A$; it is cited by [`Deformation.TraceAlgebra.descends`](thm.html#Deformation.TraceAlgebra.descends).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Matrix_span_eq_top_of_map_span_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic
import Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basis
